    # Mixed Technical Slide

    ## Release Checklist

    1. API options initialized by
       mdf_options_init.
    2. CLI validates --transition
       before rendering.
    3. MDF_FORMAT_HTML output
       remains unchanged.
    4. MDF_FORMAT_HTML_DECK emits
       deck shell, CSS, and
       JavaScript.

    > The deck renderer may
    > materialize one slide at a
    > time, but ordinary HTML mode
    > should not inherit deck-only
    > behavior.

    # Thematic Break Edge Cases

    The next fenced block contains
    a line that looks like a slide
    separator:

    Paragraph before a thematic b…
    ---
    Paragraph after a themati…

    The deck must keep this entire
    fenced block on one slide.

    # Quoted Thematic Break

    > This quote contains a
    > thematic-looking line:
    >
    > ---
    >
    > It is quoted content and
    > should remain on the current
    > slide.

    The actual slide separator is
    the unquoted thematic break
    after this slide.

    # List Thematic Break

    - List item before an indented
      thematic-looking line.

      ---

    - List item after the indented
      line.

    The indented line belongs to
    the list context and should
    not split slides unless the
    Markdown parser classifies it
    as a block-level thematic
    break outside the container.

    # Raw HTML

    <p
    data-deck-fixture="raw-html">Raw
    inline HTML is escaped and
    rendered as text according to
    existing HTML renderer
    rules.</p>

    <details> <summary>Disclosure
    content</summary> This is
    intentionally shown as escaped
    text rather than a live
    disclosure. </details>

    # Links And Interaction

    Primary documentation link
    (https://example.com/docs)

    A longer link label that wraps
    across lines in narrow
    viewports
    (https://example.com/docs/deck/
    mod
    e/long/link)

    Link activation should not
    accidentally advance the deck.
    Focus should remain usable on
    the current slide only.

    # Image Syntax

    !Tiny transparent pixel
    (data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlh
    AQA
    BAAAAACw=)

    This exercises Markdown image
    output without requiring
    network access. The image is
    intentionally tiny so it does
    not dominate the slide.

    # Long Word Pressure

    The renderer should avoid
    layout explosions from a long
    token:

    supercalifragilisticexpialido…

    Normal prose after the long
    token should remain visible.

    # Escapes And Entity Text

    Escaped punctuation should
    remain readable as literal
    text: *not emphasis*,
    [not a link], and
    # not a heading.

    Entity-looking text should
    also remain readable: AT&amp;T
    , &lt;tag&gt;, and 10&nbsp;000
    .

    ## Second-Level Slide Header

    This slide starts with a ##
    ATX heading instead of #. The
    deck renderer should still
    treat it as the slide header
    and keep the body content
    below it.

    ### Third-Level Slide Header

    This slide starts with a ###
    ATX heading. It verifies that
    lower-level first headings can
    act as slide headers without
    inheriting body centering
    behavior.

    # Final Slide

    ## End State

    This slide verifies End, G,
    URL hash restoration, and
    slide number rendering near
    the end of the deck.
